cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Win32 window transparency"
message: "If you use this reference code, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Weggemann
    given-names: Jens
repository-code: "https://github.com/jeweg/win32-window-transparency"
abstract: >-
  How per-pixel window transparency works on Windows 10/11, with a small
  Win32/C++ demo and a screenshot for each claim: the DWM opt-in with
  DwmEnableBlurBehindWindow, what GDI writes into the alpha channel,
  premultiplied alpha, DXGI swapchain models and DirectComposition, Vulkan
  with VK_COMPOSITE_ALPHA_PRE_MULTIPLIED_BIT_KHR, OpenGL presented through
  DXGI, and the GLFW transparent framebuffer bug.
keywords:
  - win32
  - windows
  - dwm
  - transparency
  - per-pixel-alpha
  - premultiplied-alpha
  - layered-window
  - directcomposition
  - dxgi
  - vulkan
  - opengl
  - glfw
  - cpp
  - reference
